[0m[49m[38;5;9m-  97     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m verified by script rather than assumed.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+       96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m combination" therefore collapses to the single default combination; `verify.sh`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+       97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m derives this by parsing `Cargo.toml` rather than assuming it, and would enumerate
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+       98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and run the full power set if features were ever added.
[0m[49m[39m   98,  99[0m:[39m[49m 
[0m[49m[39m   99, 100[0m:[39m[49m The project builds **no binary executable** (`[lib] crate-type = ["cdylib"]`
[0m[49m[39m  100, 101[0m:[39m[49m only; the C `CMakeLists.txt` declares only `add_library(... SHARED ...)`), so the
[0m[49m[38;5;9m- 101     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m "compare C and Rust binary stdout" gate is not applicable.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "compare C and Rust binary stdout" gate is not applicable.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Two C quirks the valid-path rows had to accommodate
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both are ground truth and are matched, but they mean "valid input" does not imply
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "correct output":
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **A stored block must be the last thing in the input.** `cp_stored` rejects
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    when `bits_left / 8 > LEN`, so any trailing bytes make a stored block fail with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `"Stored block extends beyond end of input stream."` (row E12).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`cp_ptr` mis-computes the stored-block source address whenever the tail path
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    in `cp_peak_bits` has run.** It backs off by `count / 8`, but the tail branch
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    adds `s->bits_left` to `count` rather than `last_bytes * 8`, so `count`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    over-counts and the `memcpy` reads from the wrong offset. Consequently rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    C13/C14/C15 assert the decoded payload only for the word-aligned shapes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`(in_bytes - first_bytes) % 4 == 0`, where the tail path never runs) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    compare differentially otherwise.
