[1m2. [38;5;10mcp_dynamic[0m's [38;5;10muint8_t lens[288 + 32][0m overflow is deterministic, not garbage.[22m[0m[0m
The loop runs while [38;5;10mn < nlit + ndst[0m (≤ 320), but one [38;5;10mcase 18[0m adds up to 138, so [38;5;10mn[0m reaches 457. The original translation "handled" this with a zeroed padded buffer; the C actually overwrites its own [38;5;10m-O0[0m stack locals, which it re-reads on every use — so the loop rewrites its own bounds. I read the frame layout out of [38;5;10mobjdump[0m and modelled it byte-for-byte ([38;5;10mcp_dyn_frame[0m, with compile-time [38;5;10moffset_of![0m assertions). Two things fell out of that:[0m[0m
